# Agroverse Shop CI and Testing

## When to run tests

- Before committing changes to nav, footer, cart, header, or page structure
- When asked to run CI or verify visual consistency
- After adding or modifying blog posts, product pages, or navigation

## Commands

```bash
npm test              # Run all Playwright tests (starts local server)
npm run test:headed   # Run with browser visible
npm run test:resume   # Resume from last failure (smart runner)
npm run test:reset    # Reset smart runner state
```

## CI (GitHub Actions)

- **Workflow**: `.github/workflows/visual-consistency.yml`
- **Triggers**: Push/PR to main; `workflow_dispatch` (manual)
- **URL**: Beta repo → beta.agroverse.shop; Prod repo → www.agroverse.shop
- **Artifacts**: playwright-report (30d); test screenshots on failure (7d)

## Local vs CI

- **Local**: Tests hit `http://localhost:8000`. Playwright auto-starts Python `http.server` on port 8000. Ensure port 8000 is free.
- **CI (GitHub Actions)**: Tests hit live site (beta.agroverse.shop or www.agroverse.shop depending on repo).

Override local baseURL: `BASE_URL=https://beta.agroverse.shop npm test`

## Architecture

- **Playwright** runs against live site in CI (no mocking)
- **Tests**: Header/footer consistency, nav, cart, mobile menu, SEO content
